# The oldest Foundation version a project may be updated FROM.
#
# This single number is what makes managed patches retirable. A patch exists to
# move projects from some older state to the current one; once no supported
# project can still be in that older state, the patch is dead weight that still
# has to be read, reviewed, and reasoned about — and whose search string can
# re-fire years later if someone legitimately reintroduces the old value.
#
# A patch whose @since is STRICTLY OLDER than this version has, by definition,
# already been applied everywhere it could apply, and managed_patch_hygiene_check.sh
# will report it as retirable.
#
# Raising this is a support decision, not a technical one: it declares that
# projects older than this must run an intermediate update before jumping to
# current. Raise it deliberately, and note it in CHANGELOG.md.
